[CHOSEN, not recovered] vkd3d-shader 2.1 patch for the BF2 macOS port (LGPL-2.1+, as vkd3d).
SM1/2 jump lowering. 0012's array-bound unroll (for (q < Count) { if (...) break; o.t[q] = ...; })
now runs for every profile: the unrolled iterations keep their exits as flag stores, so SM1/2
flattening sees guarded blocks without jumps, as D3DX9_25's vs_1_1 output has no flow control.
Below SM3 such loops failed with E5017 ("Flattening conditional blocks with non-discard jump
instructions") and the effect layer compiled the vertex shader internally as vs_3_0.
Flattening a conditional store selects between the new value and the variable's old value.
Where no store to those components can have run before (a block-local temporary such as mul()'s
per-component result), the old value is undefined and the store keeps its new value instead: the
select read a temp register before any write, which D3D9's shader validator rejects in vs_1_1 and
ps_2_0, and a NaN there would leak through the lerp-style select. Parameters, inputs, uniforms
and globals always count as initialized.
In a loop bounded that way, D3DX9_25 drops the last iteration when every store in it overwrites
a constant 0 (zero-initialized Out.ShadowTexCoord[q]: three of four elements written, the fourth
stays 0); a last store over a non-constant value keeps the full bound. Measured with
D3DXCompileShader on the Code/Tests/sm1_jump_lowering probe cases.

